{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nplan={\\\"description\\\":\\\"Discriminator: a real PreAccept message carries two commands, the first with a 70000-byte value; after marshalling, does the implementation's own decoder recover the message, or does the truncated length make it panic? Prefix: the harness builds the message and marshals it with the implementation's codec, then unmarshals from those bytes, wrapping only the decode in recover so a panic is reported instead of killing the test. Controls: the prerequisite prints the command count, the first value's size and the wire size, and the result prints whether the decoder panicked, the panic value and the bytes left.\\\",\n \\\"claim_id\\\":\\\"C10-command-value-length-survives-the-wire\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB11-value-codec\\\"],\n \\\"harness\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"go_test\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"In-package Go test that marshals a PreAccept with an oversized first command value and decodes it with the real unmarshaller.\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"harness-only scaffolding: no replica is constructed; the message and command codecs are called directly\\\",\\\"the decode is wrapped in recover() to observe a panic; the replica reader in production has no recover around its unmarshal\\\"],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"message_built\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"message_marshalled\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"commands\\\",\\\"value\\\":2},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"first_bytes\\\",\\\"value\\\":70000}]}],\n  \\\"legality\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\",\\\"S25-defs-channels\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB11-value-codec\\\"],\n   \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The PreAccept is the message a leader sends for a proposal and it carries its commands in exactly this array form, so the input is a real protocol message.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"One message, two commands, no replica.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"the reader's own path around unmarshal is not exercised, only the decode itself\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}},\n \\\"monitors\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M1-message-shift\\\",\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH3-message-shift\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"message_shifted\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB11-value-codec\\\"],\n   \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB11-value-codec\\\"],\n    \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The event reports whether the decoder survived the message and what it had left, which is the receiver-side consequence of the truncated length.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"The message carried a value beyond the length field's range.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"reference\\\":\\\"message_built.message\\\"}],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"message_built\\\"}],\n \\\"observable_properties\\\":[{\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH3-message-shift\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"event_assertion\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"message_shifted\\\"},\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"panicked\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"message\\\"],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Decoding a message the implementation itself marshalled must not panic.\\\"}],\n \\\"uncertainties\\\":[\\\"the harness observes the decode panic rather than the replica reader terminating; the reader has no recover around its unmarshal, so the panic is inferred to end the process\\\",\\\"the shipped configuration's 1000-byte commands never reach the boundary\\\"]}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"check\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"unit-C10-command-value-length-survives-the-wire\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Third scenario for the same obligation, now on the real message path: a PreAccept carrying two commands whose first value is 70000 bytes marshals to 70063 bytes, and the implementation's own decoder panics with makeslice len out of range, leaving 15700 bytes in the buffer. The harness wraps only the decode in recover so the panic is reported rather than killing the test; the reader path in production has no recover around its unmarshal, so the panic would end the receiver's process. The trusted runner and a fresh correspondence review decide the formal outcome.\\\",\n \\\"plan_path\\\":\\\"plan-message-shift.json\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"explore_message_shift_test.go\\\",\\\"files\\\":{}}\njson.dump(plan,open('plan-message-shift.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-message-shift.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-message-shift.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
